WEBVTT

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.910
What are you doing?!

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.050
The race is tomorrow!

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.250
What are we going to do with a time like this?!

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.460
You're all messing up, too!

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.670
That's because the guy in front of me was driving so slowly!

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.210
When I drove, the tires weren't warmed up yet.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.460
The seat position wasn't the same as usual, so...

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.930
How's it going?

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.890
Capeta-niichan!

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.450
You came at the right time.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.570
Listen to this...

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.030
It's no good.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.310
There's no chance of us winning if we participate.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.020
Can't we drive individually?

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.880
There has to be four people in each team for tomorrow's 60-minute endurance race for kids.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.490
Don't the regulations say each of you has to drive at least 10 minutes?

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.600
And everyone uses the same type of machine, right?

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.170
That's why the teamwork among the four of you will make the difference in winning.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:55.780
You say that, but Mika keeps messing up at the important moments.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.810
There's no point in giving it your all when someone else messes things up.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.880
Kunimitsu and Katsuyoshi both drive around as they please and spin as well.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.670
Hang on a second.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.150
Everyone follows up on one person's mistake.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.770
That's the team, right?

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:14.070
Rather than thinking of who's dragging you behind, think of how you could drive best...

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.350
and in what order you should hand over the baton.

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:21.520
It may be hard to shorten your time around the course by even one second,

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.110
but you could shorten it a second by improvising on the way you pass the baton.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.050
I see.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.090
Like Capeta-niichan said,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.720
maybe we were a little self-centered.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.610
Let's try a little harder.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.020
First we have to overcome our faults.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:36.580
Yeah.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.950
Kunimitsu!

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.480
Just try to drive so you don't spin first!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.760
Stay calm!

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.370
<i>It's the same machine, huh?</i>

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.270
<i>The same machine... on which I lost.</i>

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.230
<i>Today you will all graduate from this school.</i>

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:01.940
<i>For those who did their best these three days and have no regrets...</i>

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.200
<i>For those with regrets...</i>

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.610
<i>Everyone is different...</i>

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.610
<i>But there is one thing I can say.</i>

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.130
<i>It's the strongest who survives.</i>

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.830
<i>That's how this world works.</i>

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.250
<i>You all found this out here.</i>

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.130
<i>The experience you have gained these past three days</i>

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:21.790
<i>is worth, I believe, several years of experience for others.</i>

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:26.460
<i>The final selection process for the scholarship will be held in a month's time.</i>

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.930
<i>One of you will be selected and will move forward onto the next step.</i>

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.740
<i>Until we contact you, please stay put.</i>

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.130
<i>Now listen, Capeta.</i>

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.360
<i>Whatever you do, be careful not to crash.</i>

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:48.620
<i>They say that if you crash an FSte machine, there's no chance for you to pass.</i>

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.090
What should I do... from here on?

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.350
Even if I could race, I don't have a kart either.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.300
Okay, Naomi.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.570
Come back into the pits.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.280
<b>Understood.</b>

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.270
How's the condition of the front?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.420
Could you please go with this setting?

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.760
How's it going?

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:06.980
Mom.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.920
I had some business around here.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.380
What do you want?

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.760
Surely you don't have to make that face as though I'm in the way?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.840
Besides, we've had less time to see each other as a family these days.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.890
Ishihara looks good.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.560
I heard he got the fastest.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.770
30.85 seconds apparently.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.740
Like there's any surprise there.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:39.490
But apparently Shiba-kun from Garage Hill is one step ahead.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:42.950
Capeta-kun's machine crash in the qualifier was damaging.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:47.190
If he doesn't pass, I wonder what he'll do.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:49.230
And he probably doesn't have a kart either.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.430
Sorry.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.310
My mind is preoccupied with things here right now.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:54.490
I'll be honest.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.080
I don't care about anything else.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.120
What?

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.330
Looks good, doesn't it?

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.790
All right, let's try it with a different carburetor.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:16.900
It could still go higher.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:20.880
Boss, you have a call from the head office of FSRS.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.610
Okay.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.450
Head office of FSRS?

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.440
Come to think of it, they were saying something.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.510
That we wanted a second driver.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:37.050
Don't tell me we're going to pick up someone who flunked out of FSRS?!

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:40.080
I'm the only driver we need!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.010
Like we need a softy who's been driving karts.

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:45.010
What?!

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:48.480
Are you sure of what you just said, Tanaka-san?!

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.690
Yeah, it was my idea.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.500
Is it really true that once you get invited to the final selection,

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.900
the crash incident gets treated as if it never happened?!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.560
Well, that's if you get invited.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.990
He clearly crashed after all.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:04.650
Yes.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.180
Yes.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.380
I understand.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:08.780
That's very helpful.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.040
If you'll excuse me.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:12.550
All right.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:15.210
It's not like he's lost his chance at the scholarship yet.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:19.670
If there's any chance, we should do what we can.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.820
<i>Hang on, Capeta.</i>

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.310
<i>No matter what, I'll...</i>

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.640
Let's take a break.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.390
What would you like, Shige-san?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.610
Oh... nothing.

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:36.520
I'll pass.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.440
Again?

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.030
You should take some fluids today.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:46.050
Do you think the waves in the Atlantic and Indian oceans are harsh?

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:46.530
Huh?

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:49.130
I get seasick.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.000
What?

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.920
Capeta!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:02.630
Nobu.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:13.060
You called Tanaka-san just to find that out?

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.080
Yeah.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.560
Our chances aren't zero.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.910
Hey, Capeta.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.370
Leave everything to me.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.990
I'll do something about it.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.200
I'm sure of it.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.700
You'll become an F1 driver!

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.050
I also believe in you, Nobu.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.410
I won't start panicking.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.890
I'll leave everything to you, Nobu!

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.250
Leave it to me!

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:36.630
This is where you see your manager, Andou Nobu's skills.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:41.090
<i>I don't know what they're doing, but they're sure making the most out of their youth.</i>

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.550
<i>Sometimes I envy them.</i>

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.760
<i>Maybe I'm getting old.</i>

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.400
Okay, next.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.100
If you will, please.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:07.450
Nice work.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.380
This is next.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.530
Please.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.770
And get your make-up and hairstyle set, too.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:12.290
Yes.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.390
There.  There.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:14.900
A little bit more natural.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.770
That's good.  Let's take a shot.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:26.260
How's it going?

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.100
Photo shoots are rather tough, aren't they?

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.470
You must be tired already.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:31.560
No.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.100
This is nothing.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:58.830
From Nobu?

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.540
"About the scholarship, there's still hope!"

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.890
<b>I'll make Capeta into an F1 driver no matter what!</b>

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:07.970
<b>By Great Manager Nobu.</b>

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.930
<i>He sure is optimistic as always.</i>

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.350
<i>What's going to happen to Team Capeta?!</i>

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.400
And I'm the manager.

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:24.360
Can I continue working with the job I have now?

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.820
It's not like I'm bored with it.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:29.990
But it's just...

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.280
Thanks.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.380
So you like it.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.250
A lot!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.390
What else can you play?!

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.850
Well... there are a couple, but...

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.850
Then please play something.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.490
Let's see...

00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:59.310
Then...

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:03.830
Hey...

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.120
That was great!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.010
That wasn't bad.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.830
That was nice, wasn't it?

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.820
It sure was good.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.180
You're good at singing.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:22.540
U-Um, it was fun singing with you.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:21.420
They were really good!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.750
That was really great!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:24.230
Thank you very much!

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.230
Sing another song!

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:25.590
If you'll excuse me!

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:26.110
Encore!  Encore!

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.800
H-Hey!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.430
Wait up!

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:40.070
That sure was a surprise...

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:44.080
I didn't think I'd be suddenly doing a live street performance.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:50.650
Song...

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:52.200
Singing, huh...

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.970
All right!  Singing!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.570
I'm off to work now.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.220
I've boiled some udon, so eat it when you wake up.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.480
Yeah.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.230
I'm off.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.740
Ca-chan!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:31.930
What's the matter, Ca-chan?!

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.270
You're not happy!

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.530
If you're down like that, your luck and fortune will also run away!

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:37.560
M-Monami!

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.520
Now smile!

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:39.390
Smile!  Smile!

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:40.380
Smile!  Smile!

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.590
I-I got it.  I have work now so...

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:44.350
See you!

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:45.480
Ca-chan!

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:48.810
Let's go out there with a smile today!

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:50.720
Fight!

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.320
Good luck, Capeta!

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.570
You're so loud, Monami.

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:53.570
Go!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.780
<b>And now...</b>

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:03.900
I'll announce the results of the time trial from the qualifier.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.250
1st, Team Black Bear.

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:08.590
<b>2nd, Autohouse Kids.</b>

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:09.710
All right!

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.830
<b>3rd, Tomo-chan's.</b>

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.190
<b>4th, Dream Wheels.</b>

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.450
<b>5th, Formula Tanaka.</b>

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.980
<b>6th, Team Sarukkii.</b>

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.600
Oh man...

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.520
<b>7th, Team Hyakuanbea.</b>

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.580
In 6th place.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.510
We're 3rd from last.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:23.580
<b>8th, Heat Kids.</b>

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.140
All that practicing was for nothing!  Geez...

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.270
H-Hey, everyone...?

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:30.160
The time in the qualifier is based on the fastest driver in the team.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.900
Don't be down from the start.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:35.740
Even when our teamwork was good...

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.000
That's right.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.240
And there's no hope of winning with a total of slow times either.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.900
But you won't know until you give it your best.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:44.950
Capeta-kun.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.780
Nanako-san.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.410
Do you have time?

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.370
How are you doing as a team manager?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.670
Manager?!  It's nothing like that.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:56.490
It just happened.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:59.630
But we're the home team, so I'd like them to do well in the finals...

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.420
That's so like you, Capeta-kun.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.800
As always.

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:07.290
Hey, Capeta-kun.

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:10.270
If it's all right with you, would you like to join our team?

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:16.550
Naomi isn't around anymore and I would like you to teach our young drivers a thing or two.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.090
And you could also continue racing.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:22.740
Or are you saying it's none of my business?

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.440
I see.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:27.890
Then it can't be helped.

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:29.960
Let me know if you ever change your mind.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:31.430
Listen.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.380
There's something I'd like to say.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:36.220
Whatever you do, don't give up racing.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:36.960
Umm...

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.840
Thank you very much.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.090
Bye.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:45.760
<b>The finals will start soon in the best conditions today!</b>

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:47.970
Okay.  Take deep breaths.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:55.900
Everyone else is nervous like you, got it?

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:56.980
Yes.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.700
Team Sarukkii!  Let's go!

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:01.360
Yeah!

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:06.000
<b>It's finally time for the 60-minute endurance race for kids!</b>

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:11.750
The battle will start momentarily.

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:13.860
<b>And we finally start!</b>

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:16.270
Go, Mika!

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:17.460
Do your best!

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:23.590
<b>They all head towards the 1st corner in a ball!</b>

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:32.760
They're going to pass her!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.010
It's no good after all!

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.180
No!  It's okay.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.710
She's holding them back somehow!

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:47.870
<i>Don't rush!</i>

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:56.020
<b>Oh no!  #4, Team Sarukkii,
suddenly goes off the course!</b>

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:58.000
<b>It's a painful spin!</b>

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.140
We're in last now.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:03.980
There's no way we can catch up with them now.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:04.750
Mika!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.430
You can retire now!

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.570
The race has just started!

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.100
Are you giving up already?

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:13.900
But we're already more than half a lap behind.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.860
It's impossible.  There's no way we can catch up.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.820
I wonder...

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:24.400
It looks as though Mika-chan hasn't given up yet.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:27.570
She's probably driving by believing in you all.

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:34.160
Okay.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:35.580
Let's do what we can!

00:17:35.960 --> 00:17:36.930
You're right.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.540
And now we can drive with more ease.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.060
All right!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:41.540
Go!

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:42.250
Go, Mika!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.170
You did your best.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.700
You did well, Mika.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:48.760
No worries.

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.670
We're counting on you, Satoru!

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:52.050
Do your best!

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.490
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:55.980
Because of me...

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.690
You did great by not giving up.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:02.220
Don't worry about it.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.200
We'll get it back for you.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:05.780
The race starts from here.

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:07.150
<b>Oh no!</b>

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:11.740
<b>Autohouse Kids and Black Bear,
 who were fighting at the top, have crashed!</b>

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:14.700
<b>We've gone completely back to the start now!</b>

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:18.990
<b>Now all teams have a chance at going for the win!</b>

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.430
No way!

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:20.210
Just like Capeta-niichan said!

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.920
All right!

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:22.820
What?!

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:23.880
Singing?!

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:24.920
Yes.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.380
I've decided!

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:30.050
But you're going on track as a gurabia model, and...

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.050
What's going on?

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:36.000
At first I started this because I wanted money.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.270
But now I've found something that I really want to do.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.620
Since you've already decided,
I suppose there's no turning back.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:46.470
Okay.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:47.440
Let's give it a try.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:53.240
In return, the lessons will be much harder.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.450
Thank you very much!

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:01.500
<b>40 minutes have now passed!</b>

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:04.170
<b>We're finally at the last stage!</b>

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:08.130
<b>Team Black Bear is at the top, followed by Autohouse Kids.</b>

00:19:08.700 --> 00:19:09.840
And...

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.800
Let's go!

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:15.100
<b>What's this?!</b>

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:20.520
<b>Team Sarukkii, who dropped to last, has now risen to 3rd place!</b>

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.090
Go, Kunimitsu!

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.030
Do your best!

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:21.150
We're counting on you!

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.310
Really?!

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:27.100
Capeta—

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.170
No...

00:19:28.170 --> 00:19:30.490
Taira has been chosen for the final selection?!

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:32.100
Yes!  Yes!

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.120
I understand!

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.630
Thank you very much!

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:44.720
Go!

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:46.340
Do your best!

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:46.340
Go!

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:47.800
There!

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:55.890
<b>Team Sarukkii passes Autohouse Kids!</b>

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:55.890
We did it!

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:55.890
All right!

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.020
Capeta!

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.080
You did it!  You did it!

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.150
You did it!  You did it!

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:02.460
You did it!

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.470
You did it!  You did it!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.570
Capeta.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.280
Oh yeah.  I have to tell Capeta.

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:13.590
He's at Unbara today, right?

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.740
<b>Now there's only one corner remaining.</b>

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:26.840
<b>Who will win?!  Is it Team Black Bear, Autohouse Kids, or Team Sarukkii?!</b>

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.550
What are you doing?!

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:32.510
Pass them, Kazu!

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.090
<b>The fight is now at the last straight!</b>

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.460
<i>Capeta!</i>

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:41.460
<i>Ca-chan!</i>

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.440
<i>Go, go!</i>

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.440
<i>Last spot!</i>

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:44.950
<i>Over there!  Go!</i>

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.480
Go!  Go!

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:49.400
It's the last spot!

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:55.240
<i>Racing really is great!</i>

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:59.460
<i>No matter what happens,
I'm going all the way up to the F1!</i>

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:02.230
<i>There's only the race for me!</i>

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.950
We did it!

00:22:50.730 --> 00:22:52.710
Why, Pops?!

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:55.320
Why isn't anyone lending me a machine?!

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:57.280
I don't have a chance when it comes to growth speed.

00:22:57.280 --> 00:23:00.200
I have no choice but to practice if I want to beat him!

00:23:00.840 --> 00:23:01.930
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:01.930 --> 00:23:03.200
Victory Road!

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:04.940
Open up the future!
